d 'BOOTDIAG': module to perform bootstrap and Monte Carlo post-estimation diagnostic tests for time-series regression and the ARDL family
d
d      bootdiag replaces the asymptotic p-values of the standard
d regression diagnostics with bootstrap and Monte Carlo p-values.
d It	runs after regress, newey, ardl, aardl, fbardl, fbnardl and
d mtnardl.    The test statistic is computed from the residuals and
d the design matrix of the fitted equation, exactly as the source
d papers    define it. Only the {it:null distribution} changes: it
d is obtained by simulation rather than from a chi-squared or F
d table.    bootdiag recovers the estimated equation from e() and
d verifies the reconstruction against the residual sum of squares
d the	 fitting command reported. If the two disagree it stops
d with an error rather than reporting a number that does not
d correspond	to the model you estimated. 
d
d KW: bootstrap
d KW: Monte Carlo
d KW: regression
d KW: ARDL
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261004
d
d Author:   Merwan Roudane, NA
d Support: email  merwanroudane920@@gmail.com
d
f bootdiag.ado
f bootdiag.sthlp
f ../_/_bd_fdbreport.ado
f ../_/_bd_graph.ado
f ../_/_bd_model.ado
f ../_/_bd_parse.ado
f ../_/_bd_prereport.ado
f ../_/_bd_report.ado
f ../l/lbootdiag.mlib
f bootdiag_example.do
